  "meta": {
    "name": "mlog-assertions-8",
    "author": "cardillan",
    "description": "\nThis mod aims to make debugging in Mindustry Logic a bit easier:[[]lightgray]\n\nEnhanced [[]accent]Vars[[]] screen: full precision values, sorting and filtering variables, copying variables to the clipboard.\n\n[[]accent]Memory[[]] screen for inspecting contents of memory blocks, using the same interface as the [[]accent]Vars[[]] screen.\n\nSettings for overriding instruction limit, by up to 1000 instructions, to make space for additional debugging code.\n\n[[]accent]Snapshots[[]] allow saving, reviewing and restoring the state of logic processors, memory blocks and other entities.\n\nA [[]accent]profiler[[]] for gathering statistics about program execution.\n\nCustom mlog instructions for performing runtime checks, logging messages, reporting errors, triggering a bbreakpoint, taking snaphots and managing profiling.\n\nVisual indication of stopped processors, processors executing a [[]accent]wait[[]] instruction, and failed runtime checks, directly on the map.\n\n[[]white]Using this mod on maps with lots of processors may impact the game's performance.[[]]\n\nSee the [[]accent]README.md[[]] file in the mod's GitHub repository for more information.\n",
    "version": "0.11.8",
    "minGameVersion": "160.5",
